 "brief": {
  "short_answer": "Claims show different lost-link actions and thresholds across models and FAA guidance. The Matrice 30T uses RTH, hover, or land with a six-second trigger and failsafe RTH nuances; the Matrice 4T uses RTH and sometimes Original Route RTH; the EVO Max 4N offers Return to Home, Hover, or Land with reconnection specifics; the Matrice 210 V1 relies on Failsafe RTH triggered after three seconds and retracing its route, with GPS weaknesses affecting return. FAA guidance emphasizes reestablishing control link and following pre-determined loss-of-link procedures, with no universal timing. These variances create gaps in a single standard lost-link procedure across platforms. ",
  "sections": [
   {
    "section": "faa",
    "label": "FAA guidance",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "FAA guidance: Describe what will be done if the hazard occurs. Try to reestablish control link connection; if not, start emergency or contingency procedures for loss of control link.",
      "citations": [
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0228",
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0227",
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0049"
      ],
      "quote": "Describe what will be done if the hazard occurs. Try to reestablish control link connection with the small unmanned aircraft. If connection cannot be reestablished, start emergency or contingency procedures for loss of control link.",
      "conditions": [
       "Loss of control link"
      ],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C005",
      "section": "faa",
      "tier": "official",
      "incident_label": null
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 30T",
    "label": "DJI Matrice 30T manual",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "Matrice 30T lost-link action can be set to RTH, land, or hover; RTH automatically activates after the remote controller signal is lost for more than six seconds and continues even if control is restored.",
      "citations": [
       "dji_m30t_manual_v22_c0032",
       "dji_m30t_manual_v22_c0033"
      ],
      "quote": "The action of the aircraft when the remote controller signal is lost can be set to RTH, land, or hover in Camera View > > > Signal Lost Action in DJI Pilot 2. If RTH is canceled following the warning, the Intelligent Battery may not have enough power for the aircraft to land safely, which may lead to the aircraft crashing or being lost.",
      "conditions": [
       "Remote controller signal loss >6 seconds",
       "Lighting sufficient and vision systems OK"
      ],
      "assessment": "supported_with_conditions",
      "claim_id": "C001",
      "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 30T",
      "tier": "manufacturer",
      "incident_label": null
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 4T",
    "label": "DJI Matrice 4T manual",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "Matrice 4T Loss of remote controller signal triggers Failsafe RTH; RTH path may be shown, with AR RTH adjustments depending on distance; if lighting conditions unsuitable, hover and Original Route RTH occur.",
      "citations": [
       "dji_matrice4_manual_v12_c0065",
       "dji_matrice4_manual_v12_c0055",
       "dji_matrice4_manual_v12_c0057"
      ],
      "quote": "Loss of remote controller signal When the remote controller signal is lost, the aircraft will automatically initiate Failsafe RTH if the Signal Lost Action is set to RTH. When the lighting and environment conditions are suitable for the vision system, DJI Pilot 2 will display the RTH path... When the lighting and environment conditions are unsuitable for the vision system, the aircraft will brake and hover, then enter Original Route RTH.",
      "conditions": [
       "RTH enabled",
       "Vision system suitability varies by lighting/env"
      ],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C002",
      "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 4T",
      "tier": "manufacturer",
      "incident_label": null
     }
    ]
   },
   {
